// C standard definitions (stddef.h)
// 
// This module is signature-only.
// 
// In Fun, most things from `stddef.h` are provided by C as typedefs/macros, so
// you typically *use the names directly* after importing this module.
// 
// Import:
// - `imp std.c.def;`
// 
// Common typedef names (all treated as numeric-compatible in Fun, except
// `max_align_t` which is an opaque named type)
// - `size_t`: unsigned integer type used for sizes/lengths.
// - `ptrdiff_t`: signed integer type used for pointer differences.
// - `wchar_t`: wide character integer type.
// - `max_align_t`: an alignment type (usually a struct) available on C11+.
// 
// Optional / platform-specific typedefs
// - `rsize_t`: bounds-checked library size type (Annex K), numeric-compatible
// if provided by the platform.
// 
// Variadic arguments
// - `va_list`
// - Opaque type used with `<stdarg.h>` macros.
// 
// Common macros
// - `NULL`
// - Null pointer constant. In Fun code, prefer the `nil` literal for null
// pointer assignment and comparisons; `NULL` is also accepted (treated as the
// literal `0`) for parity with C sources (best-effort).
// 
// Notes
// - Function-like macros such as `offsetof(type, member)` require a C type
// name rather than a runtime value, so they can't be expressed as Fun
// signatures.
